infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two jobs of a TS build: transpile vs type-check
  desc Bundlers do only the first; tsc --noEmit is the separate gate for the second
  compares
    - label Transpiler
      children
        - label esbuild / swc / babel
        - label Never type-checks — erases types unverified
        - label One file at a time, no cross-file view
        - label 10-100x faster than tsc
        - label Emits JS — the shipped bundle
    - label Type checker
      children
        - label tsc --noEmit
        - label Whole-program type-check
        - label Sees every file — cross-file analysis
        - label Slow — builds the full program graph
        - label The CI gate — emits nothing (owns .d.ts)
theme
  palette #f59e0b #14b8a6
